00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.875
Okay, so moving on to Episode 4 business

00:00:55.875 --> 00:01:00.477
I thought I'd mention just a few behind the scenes facts, like a few Easter Eggs about the episode upfront

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:04.080
The fighting style of the Kyoshi Warriors is based on ninjutsu

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.260
taking your opponent's force and using it against them

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.586
In case you're not Beatles fans, or you're not old enough to remember

00:01:10.586 --> 00:01:14.893
The scene where Aang is running around in and out of frame-the montage-is based on Hard Day's Night

00:01:14.893 --> 00:01:17.180
the music video that the Beatles made

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:20.122
Even thought it sounds a little silly, I'll say careful for spoilers from the episode

00:01:20.122 --> 00:01:21.362
So moving in on Top Five moments

00:01:21.515 --> 00:01:23.835
Number 5: Welcome to Kyoshi Island

00:01:23.835 --> 00:01:26.396
So if you look at the map of the Avatar world 

00:01:26.396 --> 00:01:28.728
Kyoshi Island is right here-it's part of the Earth Kingdom

00:01:28.728 --> 00:01:31.377
It's main utility is being a fishing fort

00:01:31.377 --> 00:01:36.996
It was the place Avatar Kyoshi was born, but it's not named Kyoshi Island just because she was born there

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:40.594
The Kuvira-so to speak- of her time was named Chin the Conqueror

00:01:40.594 --> 00:01:42.634
He was trying to conquer the Earth Kindgom too

00:01:42.722 --> 00:01:48.802
In order to stop him, Kyoshi earthbent the peninsula of her hometown away from the mainland

00:01:48.802 --> 00:01:50.959
And thus it became Kyoshi Island

00:01:50.959 --> 00:01:53.961
It's a good example of how powerful the Avatar can be

00:01:53.961 --> 00:01:56.754
It's like Korra eating the full blast from the Spirit Vine Gun

00:01:56.754 --> 00:02:02.806
You have bending, you have super-bending-you have super awesome benders like Azula-and then you have the God-level bending of the Avatar

00:02:02.806 --> 00:02:05.742
It's a little unclear why Aang wanted to stop over

00:02:05.742 --> 00:02:09.363
He-he started to lose focus, see shiny objects. gets distracted very easily

00:02:09.363 --> 00:02:13.895
So you could argue he stopped because he wanted to ride the giant Koi-he just remembers them from his time

00:02:13.895 --> 00:02:15.957
Or you could argue it's an Avatar thing

00:02:15.957 --> 00:02:18.412
And his previous life as Avatar Kyoshi 

00:02:18.412 --> 00:02:21.637
is what's drawing him to the island unconsciously

00:02:21.637 --> 00:02:24.497
Sometimes there are those moments in episodes where Aang is like

00:02:24.497 --> 00:02:26.388
"I  think I remember this froma  previous life"

00:02:26.388 --> 00:02:29.427
But I bet that goes on all the time unconsciously

00:02:29.427 --> 00:02:31.327
You always wonder what goes on in people's heads

00:02:31.327 --> 00:02:35.120
It's a little easier to spell that out in a comic book or a book with a thought bubble

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.606
Whenever it's animated like this

00:02:36.606 --> 00:02:37.871
Whenver it's visual on screen

00:02:37.871 --> 00:02:41.472
You just have to fill their heads with thoughts that you think that they're thinking

00:02:41.472 --> 00:02:43.761
So I do imagine when Aang sees a lot of places

00:02:43.761 --> 00:02:47.086
he's thinking about them through the context of his previous lives

00:02:47.086 --> 00:02:48.864
even if he's not realising it

00:02:49.163 --> 00:02:51.483
Number 4: Meet the Kyoshi Warriors

00:02:51.483 --> 00:02:54.089
As the name implies, the Kyoshi Warriors were an order

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.560
born by Avatar Kyoshi

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.247
She saw some women being mistreated by men

00:02:58.247 --> 00:03:00.607
So she formed the order as a response to that

00:03:00.607 --> 00:03:03.492
It all went down way before she separated the peninsula

00:03:03.492 --> 00:03:06.193
form the mainland-so it was before it became Kyoshi Island

00:03:06.193 --> 00:03:09.561
The reason they continue to dress like her is because they want to honour their memory

00:03:09.561 --> 00:03:12.147
And you didn't need any special background to join them

00:03:12.147 --> 00:03:13.680
you could have come from any discipline

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.600
you could be a fisherwoman, you could be a housewife, anything

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:21.649
Even though there's a lot of missing data on all the Avatars, I'd say  of all the ones we do know about

00:03:21.649 --> 00:03:23.800
Avatar Kyoshi was the most proactive

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.030
She formed the Kyoshi Warriors, formed Kyoshi Island

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:30.048
And she formed the Dai Li, even though that kinda went sideways

00:03:30.057 --> 00:03:31.817
We don't blame her for that

00:03:31.817 --> 00:03:35.761
Number 3: Meet Suki-Newest member of Team Avatar-unofficially

00:03:35.895 --> 00:03:39.255
I wouldn't say Suki officially joined Team Avatar till much later

00:03:39.255 --> 00:03:41.676
This was like her soft introduction to the group

00:03:41.676 --> 00:03:44.615
I know that everyone was really bummed that she didn't appear on Legend of Korra

00:03:44.615 --> 00:03:47.843
But just look a the comics, that's what the comics are for

00:03:47.843 --> 00:03:51.993
Next to Katara, she's the next strong female to be introduced in the series

00:03:51.993 --> 00:03:56.358
Even though this is Last Airbender-so it's mostly focused on Aang-male protagonist

00:03:56.358 --> 00:03:58.322
All the women are still really strong

00:03:58.322 --> 00:04:00.468
I felt kinda bad for Sokka in this episode

00:04:00.468 --> 00:04:03.895
because they kinda use him to show how women can be that strong

00:04:03.895 --> 00:04:06.542
Gender roles-generally a really touchy subject

00:04:06.542 --> 00:04:08.152
no matter how you address it

00:04:08.152 --> 00:04:09.700
Obviously they take the comedy route

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.472
So Sokka totally works well in that context

00:04:12.472 --> 00:04:14.913
And I totally get why they had to make him sound so dumb

00:04:14.913 --> 00:04:16.861
Of all the cringe worthy scenes though

00:04:16.861 --> 00:04:19.840
I'd say the one where he first goes to try and train with them

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.978
like hey, I'm looking to work out-probably my favourite

00:04:22.978 --> 00:04:26.620
And if you are a little put off at how Sokka goes a so nuts in this espidoe

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.907
I mean, you have to remember, they're like middle school aged

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.620
And it's usually weirder 

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.200
When a middle school kid-like someone who's 11, 12, 13

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.220
is really mature, that's weird

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.586
usually you'd expect them to be really inappropriate

00:04:38.586 --> 00:04:40.840
They don't really get into it in this episode

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.064
But Kyoshi Warriors, one of their big skills

00:04:43.064 --> 00:04:46.660
Is Chi-Blocking, which totally carried forward into Legend of Korra

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.122
Obviously, there are a lot of people all of the world who practice Chi-Blocking

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:52.574
So you get Amon's Chi-Blockers and their awesome costumes

00:04:52.574 --> 00:04:55.395
I can't imagine that they stole that from the Kyoshi Warriors

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:58.590
Number 2: Surfer Aang Rides the Unagi

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:01.907
This was almost like another beach episode, inside another episode

00:05:01.907 --> 00:05:04.180
It does feel like there were a lot of those in Avatar

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.496
Like it wouldn't be a new season or a new book on Avatar

00:05:06.496 --> 00:05:09.189
Without them being on the beach doing something fun

00:05:09.189 --> 00:05:13.180
The first time in the episode, the Unagi's just teased-you don't even know it's called the Unagi

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:17.940
It's just a giant fish with a giant fin sticking out, so you're just left to wonder what's underneath the surface

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.460
And Aang, running across the water, trying to get away

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.312
Just like Korra in book 3, trying to run from the Sand Shark

00:05:23.312 --> 00:05:27.280
If you thought about it, he could run on water if he was airbending his feet

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:28.520
just like a little bit

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:32.794
Although in this context, it looks more like Roadrunner/Buggs Bunny territory

00:05:32.794 --> 00:05:36.780
Later on in the episode, I totally believe that the Avatar could form some sort of 

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.254
low level spiritual connection with other animals

00:05:39.254 --> 00:05:44.015
So I don't think it's too crazy that he could get the Unagi to breathe water all over the town

00:05:44.015 --> 00:05:48.254
It's just one of those things they don't have a lot of time to explain in a 22 minute episode

00:05:48.254 --> 00:05:53.111
And my Number 1 Moment: Aang learns what happens when you derp your mission as the Avatar

00:05:53.111 --> 00:05:55.700
There is a price to be paid for stepping off the path

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:59.155
Aang doesn't realise what's going on until he flies over the town and sees it burning

00:05:59.155 --> 00:06:02.396
But, yeah, when you get distracted, this is what happens

00:06:02.396 --> 00:06:06.399
It's a good reminder why this series didn't do too many side episodes

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:09.743
Almost the entire Kyoshi Island episode is them getting sidetracked

00:06:09.743 --> 00:06:15.151
It can be a little frustrating, especially when you know what the endpoint of the series is and you know what Aang has to do

00:06:15.151 --> 00:06:18.860
It's like why are you spending so much time over here when you need to learn how to waterbend?

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:21.191
But it's really like these sidetracked moments

00:06:21.191 --> 00:06:23.497
where they just argue about their relationshipy stuff

00:06:23.497 --> 00:06:26.680
or Aang tries to impress Katara, where their personalities come out

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:31.060
So you do need these-it helps the audience (us) form connections with the characters

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:34.672
just because they're human moments-they're things we'd totally do

00:06:34.672 --> 00:06:38.120
I would totally try to ride a Koi to impress a girl-I mean, who wouldn't?

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.620
Zuko's barely in the episode

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.380
He's just there to remind you that there's this other plot going on

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.614
But all in all, some great fight scenes

00:06:44.614 --> 00:06:47.500
great firebender versus Kyoshi Warriors scenes

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.720
It's a good way to show off what good warriors they are

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:53.080
Yes, Zuko is able to take them down really easily-but you have to remmeber

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:57.629
Of all the young characters, he's one of the few who have been extensively trained in combat

00:06:57.629 --> 00:07:01.476
Aang is very powerful, but he is not been trained in combat the way Zuko has

00:07:01.476 --> 00:07:05.125
And the funny thing is is that the episode ends with Aang getting the big payoff

00:07:05.125 --> 00:07:07.925
You know, he gets the affection from Katara that he craves so much

00:07:07.925 --> 00:07:10.880
That was probably the whole reason for him stopping

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:13.207
Is that he just wanted that hug from Katara

00:07:13.207 --> 00:07:17.980
Yes, Kyoshi Island is a really important place with some really important characters that they needed to introduce

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:20.594
So this episode was necessary for them to go there

00:07:20.692 --> 00:07:22.612
But do you think, that if Aang

00:07:22.612 --> 00:07:24.813
Was able to get that hug from Katara

00:07:24.813 --> 00:07:26.833
If he would have thought twice about stopping

00:07:26.833 --> 00:07:31.713
I do feel like half of the crazy stuff that Aang does to get attention is just to get attention from Katara

00:07:31.713 --> 00:07:32.740
Not everyone else

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:35.428
Just the girl he has a super doper crush on

00:07:35.428 --> 00:07:38.200
And I forgot to mention it at the beginning part, but another really

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:41.316
cool thing from this episode is use of Avatar maps

00:07:41.316 --> 00:07:45.053
It might sound funny, but all the funny cartoon-y maps from Legend of Korra

00:07:45.053 --> 00:07:49.020
Are meant to honour the really cartoon-y maps of Last Airbender

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:53.040
I imagine Mike and Bryan envisioned really complex, amazing-looking maps

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.735
But it ended up looking like this

00:07:54.735 --> 00:07:57.141
so when it came time to animate Legend of Korra

00:07:57.141 --> 00:08:00.403
It was just like "Hey, why don't we have fun with this and make it like Last Airbender"

00:08:00.403 --> 00:08:03.768
Favourite map sequence from either of the series though, is from Korra Book 3

00:08:03.768 --> 00:08:06.849
Whenever they're first looking for Airbenders in the Earth Kingdom

00:08:06.849 --> 00:08:10.355
I think the only real thumbs down I had in this episode was Sokka

00:08:10.355 --> 00:08:12.945
being such a derp, but I understand why they did it that way

00:08:12.945 --> 00:08:15.607
The funny thing, when you think about it, in the beginning

00:08:15.607 --> 00:08:17.140
He had this really cringe worthy line where he says

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.360
Man are more for the fighting

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:22.242
Is that later in the episode, he ends up looking like a pretty pretty woman

00:08:22.242 --> 00:08:26.219
If there's any other really fun stuff that you guys loved, be sure to put it in the comments

00:08:26.219 --> 00:08:29.484
I'll post my episode 5 video next week so be sure to subscribe to get that

00:08:29.484 --> 00:08:33.040
I'm a little happy that Game of Thrones is coming back because it's a little more fantasy

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.912
Avatar's a little more fantasy, the genres really match up

00:08:35.912 --> 00:08:40.645
So we can have Cartoons on Saturdays, with Legend of Korra, Last Airbender

00:08:40.645 --> 00:08:44.005
And then on Sundays, we can have dragons with HBO, Game of Thrones stuff

00:08:44.005 --> 00:08:47.882
In case you haven't seen it, you can click right here for my Game of Thrones trailer and you can click right here

00:08:47.882 --> 00:08:49.600
For all my other Last Airbender videos

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:53.015
Thank you so much for watching, let's all high-five, I'll see you all tomorrow

